With the following JavaScript script <link manage_application_files.csdoc>added to the application</link>...

<color JavaScript>
function sumArray(values) {
    let sum = 0;
    // use forEach to sum the values of an array
    values.forEach(value => {
        sum += value;
    });
    return sum;
}
</color>

...it is possible to pass <logiccolor>Array</logiccolor> or <logiccolor>List</logiccolor> objects due to CSPro to JavaScript <link javascript_value_conversions.csdoc>conversions</link>:

<logic>
Array someNumbersArray(4) = 10, 20, 30, 40;
List someNumbersList = 4, 6, 7, 79, 81, 82;

JS.invoke("sumArray", someNumbersArray); // 100
JS.invoke("sumArray", someNumbersList);  // 259
</logic>